# New Feature

Scaffold a new feature with the correct folder structure for **{{config.displayName}}**.

## Steps

1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for feature name and optional `--stack` flag.
2. Convert feature name to kebab-case for files and PascalCase for classes/components.
3. If no `--stack` flag, scaffold across ALL stacks in the project.

{{#ifHasStack config "next-ssr"}}
### Next.js feature

Create in `apps/{{#each config.frontend.apps}}{{#ifEquals this.type "next-ssr"}}{{this.name}}{{/ifEquals}}{{/each}}/src/features/<name>/`:

```
components/
  <Name>.tsx            -- Main feature component
  <Name>.test.tsx       -- Component test
hooks/
  use-<name>.ts         -- Feature-specific hook (if needed)
utils/
  <name>.utils.ts       -- Feature utilities (if needed)
schemas/
  <name>.schemas.ts     -- Zod validation schemas
types/
  <name>.types.ts       -- Feature TypeScript types
index.ts                -- Barrel export (public API only)
```

If the feature needs a route, also create `app/<name>/page.tsx`.
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "vite-spa"}}
### Vite React feature

Create in `apps/{{#each config.frontend.apps}}{{#ifEquals this.type "vite-spa"}}{{this.name}}{{/ifEquals}}{{/each}}/src/features/<name>/`:

```
components/
  <Name>.tsx
  <Name>.test.tsx
hooks/
  use-<name>.ts
schemas/
  <name>.schemas.ts
index.ts
```
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "nestjs"}}
### NestJS module

Create in `apps/{{#each config.backend.services}}{{#ifEquals this.type "nestjs"}}{{this.name}}{{/ifEquals}}{{/each}}/src/modules/<name>/`:

```
<name>.module.ts           -- @Module declaration
<name>.controller.ts       -- HTTP layer (thin)
<name>.service.ts          -- Business logic
<name>.repository.ts       -- Data access (if DB-backed)
dto/
  create-<name>.dto.ts     -- Input DTO with class-validator
  update-<name>.dto.ts     -- Partial update DTO
  <name>-response.dto.ts   -- Output DTO
entities/
  <name>.entity.ts         -- Domain entity
<name>.service.spec.ts     -- Unit tests
<name>.controller.spec.ts  -- Controller tests
```

Register the module in `app.module.ts` imports array.
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "go"}}
### Go feature

Add to the relevant service in `services/<service-name>/`:

```
domain/<name>.go            -- Domain model
ports/<name>_repository.go  -- Repository interface
usecase/<name>.go           -- Business logic
usecase/<name>_test.go      -- Unit tests
adapters/http/<name>_handler.go       -- HTTP handler
adapters/http/<name>_handler_test.go  -- Handler tests
adapters/postgres/<name>_repository.go      -- DB implementation
adapters/postgres/<name>_repository_test.go -- Integration tests
```

Register the handler routes in the HTTP adapter's router.
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#ifHasStack config "dotnet"}}
### .NET feature

Create in `apps/{{#each config.backend.services}}{{#ifEquals this.type "dotnet"}}{{this.name}}{{/ifEquals}}{{/each}}/Features/<Name>/`:

```
<Name>Controller.cs         -- API controller
<Name>Service.cs            -- Business logic
I<Name>Service.cs           -- Service interface
Dto/
  Create<Name>Request.cs    -- Input DTO
  Update<Name>Request.cs    -- Update DTO
  <Name>Response.cs         -- Output DTO
Validators/
  Create<Name>Validator.cs  -- FluentValidation
Entities/
  <Name>Entity.cs           -- EF Core entity
<Name>ServiceTests.cs       -- Unit tests
```

Register services in DI: create `Add<Name>Feature()` extension method.
{{/ifHasStack}}

{{#if config.mobile.enabled}}
### Expo feature

Create in `apps/mobile/features/<name>/`:

```
components/
  <Name>.tsx
  <Name>.test.tsx
hooks/
  use-<name>.ts
index.ts
```
{{/if}}

## After scaffolding

1. Ensure all files have correct imports and boilerplate.
2. Run `pnpm nx run-many -t typecheck` to verify everything compiles.
3. Report what was created and any manual steps needed.
